WEBVTT

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.990
This betrayal... This anger...

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:36.740
Is this how you reward your loyal retainers?!

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.670
December 5th, 767, New Holy Era

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.880
Kingdom of Hortensia, Royal Capital

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.450
What is this?!

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:14.450
Camellia's forces were instructed
to stand ready outside the castle!

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:28.120
Warriors of Camellia!
Now is the time to rise up for Rugis!

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.660
We're charging the palace!

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.790
There is no reason to fear Hortensia!

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:42.990
Have a taste of the humiliation we have suffered!

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:53.990
Stay your swords! We are brothers-in-arms with Camellia!

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:53.800
"Hortensian Knight Templar"
"Fernando Albert"

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:57.790
Silence! We are no longer brothers with Hortensia!

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.200
You leave me no choice.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.490
Why is this happening?

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:13.910
Fernando! This is terrible <i>moru</i> !

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.290
It's you...

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.240
Mariel is in trouble <i>moru</i> !

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:17.780
What?!

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:19.740
The king has been attacked <i>moru</i> !

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:20.580
That can't be!

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.200
Just hurry and come with me <i>moru</i> !

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:35.500
"Hortensian Knight Templar Captain"
"Maurice Baudelaire"

00:02:30.490 --> 00:02:36.160
Damn. For Camellia to turn on us
is the worst case scenario.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:41.180
"Hortensian Knight Templar"
"Adelheid Olivier"

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:41.330
Negotiations between His Majesty
and Duke Rugis must have broken down.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.790
Adelheid! Maurice!

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:44.580
Brother!

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.080
Fernando, thank goodness you're safe.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.410
Camellia is--
Duke Rugis is staging a rebellion!

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:53.540
Is that what this is?

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.870
His Majesty and the princess are in danger.

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.870
I'm going to need your help.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:00.870
Right.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:03.330
<i>Moru</i> ?

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.540
What's this now?

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.450
That's a Cerberus!

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.790
The monster of Magonian lore?

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.490
This isn't possible!

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:20.410
What in the world is happening in this land?

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:23.910
I'll deal with this.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.450
You two go save His Majesty!

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.740
Fernando, let's hurry <i>moru</i> !

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.740
We will protect His Majesty at any cost!

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:33.370
We'll leave you to it, Adelheid.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:34.910
Please do.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:43.620
Majesty!

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.330
Princess Mariel!

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.370
Father...

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.240
We were too late.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.950
Mariel...

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:51.950
Leon!

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:54.700
What happened?

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.910
Run... Take the princess...

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:02.370
We're not leaving you here.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:08.490
Fernando... please... stop him for me...

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:16.620
Leon...! No!

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.790
Princess, this way.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.540
Maurice, behind you!

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:26.120
Maurice!

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.330
Fernando!

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.790
What's going on here?!

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:40.080
What happened?! Answer me!

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.370
No! Run away!

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.040
Brother...!

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:56.950
We cannot allow the light
of Hortensia's hope to go out.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:59.490
On my code of chivalry,

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.660
I swear I will stop you!

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:03.700
I will protect the princess!

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.330
Fernando!

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.660
No!

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:24.040
Is that...?

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.700
Who could be knocking this late at night?

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:33.620
It's Dad!

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:34.580
Huh?

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.700
Dad has come back.
Nonnoria, go get a fire started.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.870
Very well!

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.120
Dad!

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:47.540
Sorry, but I'm not my brother.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.950
Uncle Maurice...

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:56.540
I'm away for a little while,
and look how much you've grown, Alfred.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:00.040
Uncle, why do you have Dad's sword?

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.790
Where is Dad? He's coming back here, right?

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:09.910
I'm sorry.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.410
Oh, no...

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:17.160
It can't be...

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.490
No, it can't be, Dad!

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.450
It can't be!

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:09.830
On the Iepetas Peninsula lay Hortensia,
a great kingdom more than 700 years old.

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:13.200
While Hortensia was continually
haunted by the threat of invasion

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.290
from surrounding nations
who desired its fertile soil,

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:22.660
its two principalities of Olivier and Camellia

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:28.040
served as its sword and shield,
allowing it to remain unravaged by war.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:33.540
And then came December 5th, 767, New Holy Era.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:37.330
Grand Duke Rugis F. Camellia,
of the principality of Camellia,

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:42.830
"Camellia Grand Duke"
"Rugis F. Camellia"

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:40.870
rose up in revolt against
the kingdom without warning.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.540
Although an overthrow
of the capital was prevented,

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:48.950
the king of Hortensia was slain,
and Princess Mariel had gone missing,

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:53.700
leaving her younger brother,
Prince Charlot, to assume the throne.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:57.260
"Hortensia's new king"
"Charlot de Hortensia"

00:08:55.080 --> 00:09:00.240
The rebellion came just as monsters
began appearing around Hortensia,

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:05.160
ushering in an age of turmoil...

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:10.770
December 23rd, 767, New Holy Era
Albert Feudal Manor

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:12.580
What we saw when we charged into the throne room

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:16.580
was a giant werewolf, straight out of legend.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:19.950
Your old man didn't back down one step,

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:24.240
and fought to his last breath
to protect the princess.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:28.950
Fighting for as long as he lived
in defense of the country--

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:32.120
that sounds like how Dad would meet his end.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:36.080
Are you all right?
You don't have to do this all at once.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:40.200
From here on, I'm going to have to govern Albert.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.830
I can't just sit around crying forever.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:46.200
Besides, I made Dad a promise--

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:49.950
that I would become a great knight, like he was.

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:52.040
Alfred...

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:56.040
Uncle, would you mind training me right now?

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.990
I need to refine my
swordsmanship skills some more.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:01.700
Fine by me. But before we get to that,

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:05.080
from now on, I want you to call me Maurice.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.040
Huh?

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:09.040
It doesn't sound right for you to call me Uncle

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.950
when you're the lord around here, does it?

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:13.080
What do you mean, I'm the lord?

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:17.330
I'm resigning from the royal order,
and staying here in Albert.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:20.370
Settling down here and serving
my nephew doesn't sound so bad.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.040
Do you really mean it, Uncl--

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:28.160
I'm looking forward to it, my lord.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.660
Thank you, um... Maurice.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:35.240
Yeah, there you go.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:40.660
Th-Th-This is terrible! Marius is gone!

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:46.290
He had finally gotten up and around, too!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.200
Did he run away? Did he run away?

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:51.410
I don't think we have to worry about that.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:55.160
But still, he didn't say anything!

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:58.330
This has been hard on him, too.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:00.740
Let's just leave him be for now.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:13.660
Marius, you'll worry the others
by strolling around on your own moru.

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:15.830
Let's go back <i>moru</i> .

00:11:15.830 --> 00:11:18.870
Sorry, but could you leave me to myself?

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:20.700
<i>Moru</i> ...

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:32.700
I heard that Marius was burned out
of his home during that rebellion.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:37.240
He'd lost his family,
and your old man helped him out.

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:50.830
Father, Fernando, Leon... they're all dead.

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:57.120
Charlot, I'm sorry. You're all alone now.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.370
So this is where you went.

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:03.160
Alfred...

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:08.080
It looks like you're feeling better now.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.240
Mm-hmm.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.330
Do you not like living here?

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:13.200
No, it's not that.

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:17.490
I hear you lost your family, too.

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:23.700
This is my family's gravesite.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:27.870
My mom and sister...

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:34.160
And pretty soon, my dad will be buried here.

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:37.540
Dad always put his life on the line

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:40.950
and stuck to his code of chivalry,
no matter who he was facing.

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:45.200
To protect the princess... and all of Hortensia.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.830
I never thought...

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:55.160
I never thought things would end up like this!

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:03.790
Neither did I. How could this happen?

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:09.160
You've been through a lot
of hardship too, haven't you?

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:14.490
And yet you're still alive.
It's hard on me that I've lost my dad,

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:16.740
but it's not as though I've lost all hope.

00:13:19.160 --> 00:13:21.910
After all, I met you, the boy Dad saved.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:25.830
Listen, Marius,

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:30.740
we have to go on living.
No matter what hardships come our way.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:34.040
What do you want to do now?

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:36.620
I...

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.580
I...

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:47.120
I want to get stronger!

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:50.200
I need strength.

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:53.410
I don't want to stand around crying anymore!

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:02.190
4 years later

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:05.740
April 10th, 771, New Holy Era
Erp Heights

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:14.290
Once we clear this forest,
we'll be at the Erp Heights front line.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.870
According to our scout's report,
the Camellian advance force is a single platoon.

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:22.830
We're going to rendezvous
with our allies and hit them.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:28.080
Thanks, Marius.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.990
Don't get left behind, my lord.

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:34.910
You've become such a trusty squire, Marius.

00:14:34.910 --> 00:14:39.580
As your squire, I have to make up
the difference wherever you fall short.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:42.740
Alfred, I promise I will keep you safe.

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:46.580
I'll show off the skill with the sword
that Maurice drilled into me.

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:49.120
Don't get too carried away, there.

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:50.580
Maurice!

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:55.950
Our allies' forces are more than ample,
but this will be your first fight.

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:57.330
Keep on your toes.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:58.540
--Yeah.
--Right.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:02.740
Everyone, let's all get through this
alive and go back to Albert!

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:19.330
No, it can't be...

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.410
This is awful.

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:25.160
The main force has been wiped out.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.240
There's a survivor!

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:35.080
That scarlet force--it must be Roy's unit.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:35.950
What?!

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:38.450
Camellia's vaunted elite archer unit.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:41.290
Split up into platoons and see to the survivors!

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.450
Let's go, Marius!

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:43.700
Right!

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:45.240
Hey!

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:47.370
Are you all right? We'll get you out right now.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:49.290
Thank you...

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:50.790
It's an ambush?!

00:15:57.490 --> 00:15:58.700
Leave them to us! Retreat!

00:15:58.700 --> 00:15:59.470
But sir!

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:00.490
Hurry!

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:06.330
Damn it!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.450
Marius!

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.200
Are you all right, Marius?

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:25.540
This was nothing.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.080
Huh? Where are those knights?

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:29.120
Over there.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:32.200
Right...

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:33.580
You saved me.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:40.290
How far the Hortensian knights have fallen.

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:46.370
For your crime of casting
your pride upon the ground,

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:48.150
"Camellian Troop Commander"
"Roy Bachelot"

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:49.040
you will pay with your lives.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.580
You're Roy, aren't you?!

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:53.700
That sword--

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:57.330
I see. The keepsake of Sir Fernando.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:01.120
You must be the young lord of Albert.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:05.490
They had lost their will to fight.
You didn't have to kill them!

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:08.370
This is the battlefield.

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:13.040
If you can spout something as ridiculous as that,
then you must be quite the fool indeed.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:16.120
You take back what you just said!

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:18.160
As if surviving is anything to be ashamed of!

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.200
What Alfred said is not wrong!

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:21.330
Don't overdo it, Marius!

00:17:21.330 --> 00:17:25.540
You would risk your life to defend
a lord without knightly resolve?

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:30.700
I do not think he is deserving of such loyalty.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:31.790
Marius!

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:38.200
You are inexperienced.
If Sir Fernando were still alive,

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.620
how great would his lament be!

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:43.200
What do you know about my father?!

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:49.990
Ho, it appears you have some spine after all.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:55.830
You're finished.

00:17:58.330 --> 00:17:59.330
Why, you...!

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:01.540
I will protect my lord...

00:18:01.540 --> 00:18:04.660
...my dear friend, no matter what!

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:07.160
Then I'll start with you!

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:08.330
Stop!

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:17.120
Stop, Roy!

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:20.200
Maurice?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.620
You got off without having your comrades die for nothing.

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:24.830
Roy!

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.580
We've accomplished enough. We're leaving.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:30.790
Sir!

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:34.370
All troops, fall back! Look alive!

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:35.370
Damn!

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:47.950
Where am I?

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:50.450
Thank goodness!

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:55.330
Thank goodness! Marius!

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:59.410
You didn't wake up for so long, I was worried!

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:01.490
Sorry, Nonnoria.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.540
Where is Alfred?

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:17.370
Dad, why did you become a knight?

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:21.910
Hmm... to protect the ones I love, I suppose.

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:24.370
The ones you love?

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:29.700
The king and people of this land,
my friends in the royal order, as well as...

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:33.790
...my family, who is more important to me
than anything--you and Ber.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:40.660
As long as I live, I will love you,
and be your shield of protection.

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:42.540
Which is why I want you, too,

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:47.200
to be a pure-hearted knight,
and protect those that you love.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:51.990
I'll become a knight!
I'll make your wish come true, Dad!

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:57.410
Dad left me Albert, and I swore to protect it--

00:19:57.410 --> 00:20:01.620
to protect those who live here,
and my dear friends...

00:20:02.790 --> 00:20:05.740
So this is where you are.

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:08.540
Marius? Are you okay?

00:20:08.540 --> 00:20:14.330
Yeah. It looks like the others
made it safely back to Albert, too.

00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:16.240
So don't be so discouraged.

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:18.660
That's not good enough.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:23.540
Even doing all that I can now,
I still can't protect anything.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:26.910
I have to get stronger.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:30.660
Not just my skill with the sword, either.
I want greater strength.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:33.700
Don't go thinking that you
can get stronger alone.

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:34.700
Marius...

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:40.160
I am your squire.
I'm going to get stronger, too! So...

00:20:40.160 --> 00:20:43.120
...don't go trying to take all of this on yourself.

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:47.120
Thanks, Marius.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:50.700
Now that that's clear,
we should be getting back.

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:53.620
Everyone is waiting for your return.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.990
Alfred!

00:20:55.990 --> 00:20:57.790
Marius!

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:08.580
The kingdom's historic tragedy
brought these two together,

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:14.450
which would in time bring about
a new era to this world.

00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:18.450
However, the pair were yet unaware
of the forthcoming harsh fighting

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:21.450
that was waiting for them.

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.080
Chapter 1

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.080
Resolve

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:31.080
~The Conflict with Camellia~

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:05.540
The border forces have been wiped out.

00:23:05.540 --> 00:23:09.080
Hortensia will not be taking any
action against us for some time.

00:23:09.080 --> 00:23:13.080
This should also serve as an example to Dayereh.

00:23:13.080 --> 00:23:15.450
Good work.

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:18.790
Rugis, I do have something else to report.

00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:20.450
What is it?

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:23.240
I came across Sir Fernando's keepsake.

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:29.330
Well, now I have something to look forward to.

00:23:32.580 --> 00:23:34.950
So it shouldn't be any wonder that
the monster of Tron Cavern is real.

00:23:34.950 --> 00:23:36.870
I wish I could do as much as you, Nonnoria.

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:41.450
No, no! Marius, you still have
a lot on your shoulders!

00:23:41.450 --> 00:23:42.910
I can't stand wolves.

00:23:42.910 --> 00:23:47.080
But right now, time is of the essence!

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:47.070
Chapter 2

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:47.070
Memories

00:23:44.080 --> 00:23:47.070
~The Lore of Magonia~
